**1. Simple if Statement:**

**Syntax:**
```java
if (condition) {
    // Execute if condition is true
}
```

**Example:**
```java
int age = 20;
if (age >= 18) {
    System.out.println("You are an adult");
}
// Continues after if block regardless
```

**Use Case:** Execute code only when condition is true

**2. if-else Statement (Two-way Decision):**

**Syntax:**
```java
if (condition) {
    // Execute if true
} else {
    // Execute if false
}
```

**Example:**
```java
int number = 7;
if (number % 2 == 0) {
    System.out.println("Even");
} else {
    System.out.println("Odd");  // This executes
}
```

**Use Case:** Choose between two alternatives

**3. if-else-if Ladder (Multiple Conditions):**

**Syntax:**
```java
if (condition1) {
    // Execute if condition1 is true
} else if (condition2) {
    // Execute if condition2 is true
} else if (condition3) {
    // Execute if condition3 is true
} else {
    // Execute if all conditions are false (default)
}
```

**Example:**
```java
int score = 85;
if (score >= 90) {
    System.out.println("A");
} else if (score >= 80) {
    System.out.println("B");  // This executes
} else if (score >= 70) {
    System.out.println("C");
} else {
    System.out.println("F");
}
```

**Use Case:** Choose from multiple alternatives

**Important Rules:**

**Order Matters:**
```java
// WRONG - General before specific
int score = 95;
if (score >= 60) {
    System.out.println("Pass");  // Executes (wrong!)
} else if (score >= 90) {
    System.out.println("Excellent");  // Never reached
}

// CORRECT - Specific before general
if (score >= 90) {
    System.out.println("Excellent");  // Executes first
} else if (score >= 60) {
    System.out.println("Pass");
}
```

**Only First Match Executes:**
```java
int x = 15;
if (x > 10) {
    System.out.println("Greater than 10");  // Executes
} else if (x > 5) {
    System.out.println("Greater than 5");  // Skipped!
}
```

**Best Practices:**
```java
// Always use braces, even for single statements
// AVOID:
if (age >= 18)
    System.out.println("Adult");  // Risky!

// PREFER:
if (age >= 18) {
    System.out.println("Adult");  // Safe
}

// Order conditions from most specific to general
// Check highest values first in if-else-if
```

**Common Use Cases:**
```java
// Grade calculator
if (marks >= 90) grade = "A";
else if (marks >= 80) grade = "B";
else if (marks >= 70) grade = "C";
else if (marks >= 60) grade = "D";
else grade = "F";

// Age verification
if (age >= 18) {
    System.out.println("Can vote");
} else {
    System.out.println("Too young");
}

// Range check
if (age >= 18 && age <= 65) {
    System.out.println("Working age");
}
```

