**Nested if Statements:**

**Definition:** if statement inside another if statement

**Syntax:**
```java
if (condition1) {
    if (condition2) {
        // Execute if both conditions true
    }
}
```

**Example 1: Login System**
```java
String username = "admin";
String password = "pass123";

if (username.equals("admin")) {
    if (password.equals("pass123")) {
        System.out.println("Login successful");
    } else {
        System.out.println("Wrong password");
    }
} else {
    System.out.println("User not found");
}
```

**Example 2: Eligibility Checker**
```java
int age = 25;
boolean hasExperience = true;
int years = 3;

if (age >= 21) {
    if (hasExperience) {
        if (years >= 2) {
            System.out.println("Eligible");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Need more experience");
        }
    } else {
        System.out.println("Experience required");
    }
} else {
    System.out.println("Age requirement not met");
}
```

**Alternative: Using Logical Operators**

Same logic without nesting:
```java
// With nested if (above)
if (age >= 21) {
    if (hasExperience) {
        if (years >= 2) {
            System.out.println("Eligible");
        }
    }
}

// With logical AND (simpler)
if (age >= 21 && hasExperience && years >= 2) {
    System.out.println("Eligible");
}
```

**When to Use Nested if:**

**Use Nested When:**
- Different error messages for each condition
- Need to check second condition only if first is true
- Logic has hierarchical structure

```java
// Nested - Better for different messages
if (age >= 18) {
    if (hasLicense) {
        System.out.println("Can drive");
    } else {
        System.out.println("Get a license first");
    }
} else {
    System.out.println("Too young to drive");
}
```

**Use Logical Operators When:**
- All conditions must be true for single action
- Same error message for all failures
- Simpler, flatter code is preferred

```java
// Logical AND - Better for single success/failure
if (age >= 18 && hasLicense && hasInsurance) {
    System.out.println("Can drive");
} else {
    System.out.println("Cannot drive");
}
```

**Avoid Deep Nesting (Bad Practice):**
```java
// BAD - 4 levels deep (hard to read)
if (a) {
    if (b) {
        if (c) {
            if (d) {
                System.out.println("Done");
            }
        }
    }
}

// GOOD - Use logical operators
if (a && b && c && d) {
    System.out.println("Done");
}
```

**Mixed Approach:**
```java
if (username.equals("admin") && password.equals("pass123")) {
    if (accountActive && !accountLocked) {
        System.out.println("Login successful");
    } else {
        System.out.println("Account inactive or locked");
    }
} else {
    System.out.println("Invalid credentials");
}
```

**Benefits of Nesting:**
- Specific error messages
- Early exit from checks
- Clearer logic flow

**Drawbacks of Nesting:**
- Harder to read when deep
- More indentation
- Can be simplified with &&/||

