**Common Conditional Mistakes:**

**1. Accidental Semicolon After if:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
int x = 15;
if (x > 10);  // Semicolon here!
{
    System.out.println("Greater");  // Always executes!
}

// ✅ CORRECT
if (x > 10) {  // No semicolon
    System.out.println("Greater");
}
```

**2. Missing Braces:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
if (score > 90)
    System.out.println("Great!");
    totalPassed++;  // Always executes!

// ✅ CORRECT
if (score > 90) {
    System.out.println("Great!");
    totalPassed++;  // Executes only if true
}
```

**3. Using = Instead of ==:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
int x = 5;
if (x = 10) { }  // ERROR! Assignment in condition

// ✅ CORRECT
if (x == 10) { }  // Comparison
```

**4. Wrong if-else-if Order:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG - General before specific
int score = 95;
if (score >= 60) {
    System.out.println("Pass");  // This executes!
} else if (score >= 90) {
    System.out.println("Excellent");  // Never reached
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Specific before general
if (score >= 90) {
    System.out.println("Excellent");
} else if (score >= 60) {
    System.out.println("Pass");
}
```

**5. Using OR Instead of AND:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
int age = 25;
if (age >= 18 || age <= 65) { }  // Always true!

// ✅ CORRECT
if (age >= 18 && age <= 65) { }  // Range check
```

**6. String Comparison with ==:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
String name = new String("John");
if (name == "John") { }  // Unreliable!

// ✅ CORRECT
if (name.equals("John")) { }  // Compares content
```

**7. Not Checking for null:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
String text = getText();  // May return null
if (text.length() > 0) { }  // NullPointerException!

// ✅ CORRECT
if (text != null && text.length() > 0) { }
```

**8. Missing break in switch:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
        // Missing break!
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");  // Also executes!
}

// ✅ CORRECT
switch (day) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Monday");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Tuesday");
        break;
}
```

**9. Empty if Block:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
if (score < 60) {
    // Empty
} else {
    System.out.println("Passed");
}

// ✅ CORRECT
if (score >= 60) {
    System.out.println("Passed");
}
```

**10. Variable Scope Error:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
if (score >= 60) {
    String grade = "Pass";
}
System.out.println(grade);  // ERROR! Out of scope

// ✅ CORRECT
String grade;
if (score >= 60) {
    grade = "Pass";
} else {
    grade = "Fail";
}
System.out.println(grade);  // OK
```

**11. Chaining Comparisons:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
int x = 15;
if (10 < x < 20) { }  // ERROR! Invalid syntax

// ✅ CORRECT
if (x > 10 && x < 20) { }  // Use logical AND
```

**12. Floating-Point Comparison:**

```java
// ❌ WRONG
double result = 0.1 + 0.2;
if (result == 0.3) { }  // FALSE due to precision!

// ✅ CORRECT
if (Math.abs(result - 0.3) < 0.0001) { }
```

**Prevention Checklist:**
- ✅ No semicolon after if/while/for
- ✅ Always use braces { }
- ✅ Use == for comparison, not =
- ✅ Order if-else-if from specific to general
- ✅ Use .equals() for strings
- ✅ Check for null before using
- ✅ Add break in switch cases
- ✅ Declare variables outside if when needed
- ✅ Use && for range checks, not ||

code:
public class CommonMistakes {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int score = 95;

        // WRONG order
        if (score >= 60) {
            System.out.println("Pass");  // This prints
        } else if (score >= 90) {
            System.out.println("Excellent");  // Never reached!
        }

        // CORRECT order
        if (score >= 90) {
            System.out.println("Excellent");  // This prints
        } else if (score >= 60) {
            System.out.println("Pass");
        }

        // String comparison
        String name = "John";
        if (name.equals("John")) {  // CORRECT
            System.out.println("Found");
        }

        // Always use braces
        if (score > 80) {
            System.out.println("Good");
        }
    }
}
